  body: "# Termination following suspension in the DMG\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nIn the described failure-to-provide-information
    context, the chapter treats a termination decision as a supersession carrying a right of appeal, subject to
    the surrounding conditions.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nDMG 04846 spans PDF pages 127–128: the conditions
    include full suspension, an elapsed or extended information period, and the stated revision-or-supersession
    qualification. Partial suspension is expressly distinguished. This record does not automate termination.\n\n\
    ## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 04847, PDF page 128](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a105e7a1eb143220d8d27f1/dmg-ch-04.pdf#page=128)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 4: Supersession, suspension and termination .\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted
    interpretation of the 15 September 2026 source snapshot; unreviewed and requiring specialist review. The source
    is DWP guidance, not a consolidated statement of legislation. This is an independent experimental publication,
    not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule.\n\nPDF page numbers are
    one-based file positions. Machine extraction can alter reading order, footnotes and characters. Quoted relationships
    preserve extracted text; no visual or specialist acceptance is claimed. Source dates, legal effects and current
    applicability remain separate review tasks.\n\n- `dmg-vol1-ch4` PDF SHA-256: `9c96b49a78aa4dc40df8594cf65cbd435a681d0be3737729cd87882542d0e2ea`;
    extracted pages SHA-256: `bef5fc9f04b2a78c5bb5dc99468f94a1841f1ef4afa117d47aa9c1e5040f3752`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/dmg-supersession
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The complete paragraph explicitly classifies this termination decision as a supersession.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol1-ch4/0128
      quote: "04847 The time limit of 14 days may be extended where the DM considers in all the circumstances it
        is\nreasonable to do so (see DMG 04850). A decision terminating benefit in these circumstances will be a\n\
        \nsupersession decision. This decision carries the right of appeal 1.\n\n\n                            \
        \                                      1 SS Act 98, s 23; SS CS (D&A) Regs, reg 18"
      locator: DMG 04847
  - target: term/dmg-first-tier-appeal
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The paragraph expressly states that the described decision carries a right of appeal.
    evidence:
